# What the image build must not carry. The build context is the repository, so anything left in it
# would otherwise be copied into a layer: local state, test tooling, and above all the deployment's
# own secrets, which live in mounted files and the environment and never in an image.
#
# `apps/web/dist` is ignored on purpose: the image builds its own console from the lockfile in the
# `console` stage, and excluding the authoring machine's build output is what proves it. Markdown is
# not ignored, because the frozen diagnostic contract's manifest covers its README and a normalised
# or missing copy would fail the readiness check.

.git
.gitattributes
.github
.gitignore

# Local runtime state: virtual environment, installed Node modules, and every ignored artifact.
.runtime
.venv
venv
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
playwright-report
test-results
coverage
htmlcov

# A console built outside the image is never an input to it.
apps/web/dist
dist

# Tests and developer documentation are not needed to run the service.
tests
docs

# Data and logs are runtime state, never build input.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db
*.log
*.jsonl

# Secrets and keys of every shape: a certificate or an environment file must be mounted, not baked.
.env
*.env
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
settings.json
*.settings.local.json
